Subject: wave: own standalone VLAN/source policy and association-time backhaul admission

Use the Linux bridge as the sole bridged forwarding/querier owner. Standalone
APs retain exact station/reporting-host VLAN and IGMPv3/MLDv2 source state in a
bounded host engine, with query and expiry work on the existing radio master.
Admit filtered ordinary data through exclusive, immutable firmware recipient
classes only after acknowledged membership; preserve shared command, membership,
quarantine and DAT_CFM pins. Pool or partial-admission failure remains closed.
Observe bridge upper changes without blocking the master on RTNL, and restart
standalone discovery after detach. Preserve explicit aggregate-air mode.

Consume the configured Association Response Multi-AP role through the existing
nl80211 IE_ASSOC_RESP handoff before STA_ADD, separately from bounded peer
metadata. The companion hostapd AP-template producer supplies that role; peer
IEs alone cannot authorize four-address mode. No firmware command or child GTK
context is invented.

